{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Welcome to the 10th Zend Certified Engineer in Dotboost Team{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">PHP Development</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Welcome to the 10th Zend Certified Engineer in Dotboost Team</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">

            {{ include('@partial/left-menu.html.twig') }}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">Welcome to the 10th Zend Certified Engineer in Dotboost Team</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> PHP Development
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        Today is a major milestone for our <a href="http://www.dotboost.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dotboost Technologies Inc.</a> Company. We are announcing the 10th member of the team passed the Zend Certified Engineer exam.

<a href="http://bit.ly/dotboost-zce" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zend Yellow Pages</a>

This is part of our commitment to ensure that our clients have access to top level PHP development as standard practice and allows us to follow a strong quality assurance program.
The next step is to implement the Zend Framework 2 best practices and to take the upcoming Zend Framework 2 Certified Architect exam.

Beginning 2014, a Zend Certification will became mandatory for every developer in our team.
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>

        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
